  "findings": "Compared three photographs showing a single bare stem, upper whorl of three broad bracts and three white petals, then revised current size pilots 1/4/7 and all 36 seeded instances. Replaced the generic five-petal bloom with a dedicated three-petal structure and raised the leaf whorl from mid-stem to 68 percent height. Each asset is an individual shoot, 0.20-0.40 m tall, not an invented branched flower bush. Seed rotation, lean and size retain 36 distinct voxel hashes. Three petals remain stylized block arms at 25 mm; petal waviness, stamens and venation fall below this pitch. Accepted as the spring flowering architecture.",
